  "_note": "Presentation of each location style (design/art/visual-upgrade-plan.md §2, art-bible §4.2, §6). Keyed by locations.json look.props ('ruins' = swamp) plus 'base'. Visual only: nothing here touches collision or gameplay. layers = Parallax2D background layers back to front: scale = scroll_scale.x (vertical parallax is softer), kind = procedural placeholder painter, col = base colour, fog = 0..1 mix toward the fog colour (atmospheric perspective), tex = optional res:// image that replaces the placeholder (kind stays as the fallback if the file is missing; tex_scale = its scale, it repeats every width x tex_scale px; tex_y = its top relative to ground_y; tex_mod = tint). The swamp uses the Blender renders of tools/asset-pipeline/blender/build_swamp_bg.py (rendered at 1.5x, so tex_scale 0.6667). enemy_rim = the outline / back light drawn on pre-rendered enemies above the darkness so they read in the dark. terrain = ground and platform colours; dark_tint = colour the darkness multiplies toward (plan §2.9 CanvasModulate); post = vignette / grading / glow / grain, hero_glow = alpha of the warm additive light around the hero; particles = ambient CPUParticles2D around the camera; camera = look-ahead and vertical dead zone. tex_up = px of the image's top rows stretched upward (no visible top edge). ambient = optional CanvasModulate colour (the light level 2D lights add to).",
